meta {
  name: 5 Register device token
  type: http
  seq: 5
}
post {
  url: {{gatewayUrl}}/device-token
  body: json
}
body:json {
  {
    "token": "fake-device-token-for-local-testing",
    "platform": "android"
  }
}
docs {
  ⚠️ Note the path: **`/device-token` at the root**, not under `/api/v1/auth/`. It is mapped on `app`
  directly rather than on the `api/v1/auth` group. Requires a JWT.

  ⚠️ **`platform` is matched case-sensitively** against `"android"` and `"ios"` — `"Android"` is a 400.
  This request said `"Android"` until 2026-09-06, so it had never actually registered anything.

  Registering also **takes this token away from any other account holding it**: a device token addresses one
  device, so at most one account may be reachable through it. See **6 Unregister device token** for the
  sign-out half.
}
